;; A MINT whose oneof names a member the message does not carry.
;;
;; A minted oneof names its members by FIELD NAME, because a mint declares no
;; numbers — so this is the mistake the form makes available, and it is the one
;; the generator must REFUSE rather than drop. Dropping it emits a oneof one arm
;; short, or none at all when that arm was its only member, and the emitted file
;; then reads as a policy that deliberately withheld the arm.
;;
;; `seq` is real and pinned; `absent_member` is neither. The refusal names
;; `oneof-member-absent` and lists the fields the message does carry.
{"pgbad.Ping"
 {:kind :message
  :name "Ping"
  :fields [{:name "seq" :type :uint32}]
  :oneofs [{:name "detail" :required false :fields ["seq" "absent_member"]}]}}
